-- title:
--   Satz 2 (Verschärfung des Hauptsatzes) — a point on all extreme supports is a nonnegative combination of at most $n$ points of $S$
-- statement:
--   Let $S \subset \mathbb{R}^n$ be a finite non-degenerate point system, and let $x \in \mathbb{R}^n$ satisfy every extreme support inequality of $S$: $\langle \alpha, x\rangle \ge 0$ for every extreme support $\alpha$ of $S$. Then $x$ is a nonnegative linear combination of at most $n$ points of $S$: there is a subset $T \subseteq S$ with
--
--   $$|T| \le n \qquad\text{and}\qquad x = \sum_{t \in T} c_t\, t, \quad c_t \ge 0 .$$
--
--   This sharpens the Hauptsatz (Satz 1) by bounding the number of generators needed. Combined with Satz 1 it contains the conic form of Carathéodory's theorem: every point of the cone generated by a finite spanning set $S \subset \mathbb{R}^n$ is a nonnegative combination of at most $n$ of its points.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $T$ is a sub-`Finset` of $S$ with at most $n$ elements; it is not required to be linearly independent, and the coefficients are only required to be nonnegative. The standing hypotheses of Satz 1 (finite, non-degenerate $S$) apply, as Satz 2 is stated immediately after the proof of Satz 1 about the same $S$.
-- source:
--   Weyl, Elementare Theorie der konvexen Polyeder, Comment. Math. Helv. (1935), p. 295, Satz 2 (Verschärfung des Hauptsatzes)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_WeylPolyhedra_Shared_Representable
import Definitions.Def_WeylPolyhedra_Shared_NonDegenerate
import Definitions.Def_WeylPolyhedra_Shared_IsExtremeSupport

namespace WeylPolyhedra.Pyramid

/-- Weyl (1935), §2, p. 295, Satz 2 (Verschärfung des Hauptsatzes): let `S ⊆ ℝⁿ` be a finite
non-degenerate point system. Every point `x` that satisfies all extreme support inequalities of
`S` is a nonnegative linear combination of at most `n` points of `S`. -/
theorem hauptsatz_at_most_n {n : ℕ} (S : Finset (Fin n → ℝ)) (hS : Shared.NonDegenerate S)
    (x : Fin n → ℝ) (hx : ∀ α : Fin n → ℝ, Shared.IsExtremeSupport S α → 0 ≤ α ⬝ᵥ x) :
    ∃ T : Finset (Fin n → ℝ), T ⊆ S ∧ T.card ≤ n ∧ Shared.Representable T x := by sorry

end WeylPolyhedra.Pyramid
